# Core APP Dynamic Provider Contract

See task stream `AIPIFY.CORE.APP.DYNAMIC.PROVIDER.CONTRACT.V1`.

## Permanent rules

1. **Core APP is provider-agnostic** — shared APP UI never hardcodes customer or provider names.
2. **No pilot advantages** — Unonight is an ordinary registry record, not a special APP solution.
3. **No custom customer panels** — one generic wizard for all providers.
4. Provider presentation data comes from the **canonical Core registry** (`app_portal_integration_providers.presentation_contract`).
5. **Scopes, URLs, setup steps, and help** come from the contract — never JSX/locale hardcoding.
6. The same generic components serve all live APP panels; Core updates propagate automatically.
7. Website Kompis follows the same Core presentation rule; do not open frozen Kompis runtime streams for presentation fixes unless explicitly required.
8. Provider adapters may remain **server-side**; they must not require customer-specific APP UI.
9. **Fail-closed** when the contract is missing or invalid — never fall back to Unonight or invent destinations.
10. Do not declare Production Ready from fixture-only proof; ordinary provider parity tests are required.

## Forbidden

- `if (provider === "unonight")` / `switch ("unonight")` in shared APP presentation
- Hardcoded admin URLs (e.g. `www.unonight.com/...`) in APP components or locale copy
- Hardcoded scope lists or numbered setup steps with provider proper names in UI/locale
- Parallel provider registries or local JSON as source of truth
- Custom Unonight APP wizard/error business logic

## Allowed

- Server-side provider adapters under `lib/<provider>/`
- Registry/seed data that stores display names and destinations for ordinary providers
- Generic locale templates with `{providerName}`, `{adminName}`, `{credentialName}`
